{number: 151}
{title: God Is Our Refuge Safe}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] God is our refuge safe, strength,
And our [F] present [C] aid, ever near us,
[G7] Therefore, tho' the earth be moved,
Hills midst the seas be east,
We will [C] not fear at all, For God is nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Al-[C] though the nations raged,
Although the [F] kingdoms [C] moved, conflicts swelling
[G7] Before His mighty word,
From war the nations cease,
The [C] troubled earth is stilled when voice is heard.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O [C] come behold the works,
Jehovah's [F] hand has [C] wrought on the earth here,
To [G7] utmost ends of all He causes war to cease,
He makes abiding peace in [C] every land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Be [C] still and bow in fear
And know that [F] He is [C] God, all ye nations;
To [G7] us the Lord of Hosts ever our refuge be,
A refuge strong and sure is [C] our God.
{end_of_verse}
